-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- 0039_names_rule_7 — the name rule, seventh version (S-03, phase 1b). 0039_names_rule_6.sql is applied and never edited; this file
-- runs right after it (the same number: 0040–0069 belong to other branches) and replaces the rule's generated functions.
--   Found after 0039_names_rule_6 (verifier round 6, v-spoof6-r1): a mark that the fonts draw BESIDE its letter reads as an apostrophe
--   next to it. Slovak and Czech ď ľ ť Ľ draw the caron as ’ after the letter, so «Paľo Kováč» and «Pal’o Kováč» were the same to the
--   pixel in the bold thread list and the chat header (EN and AR, 1440 and 390) while their skeletons differed («palokovac» /
--   «pal'okovac»): the picker offered the look-alike first, with the same company and city and no ⚠️, and a message reached it. The
--   same family: Greek capitals with the tonos or a breathing at their upper left («Άννα Νίκου» / «’Αννα Νίκου», «Όλγα» / «’Ολγα»),
--   «Marie ďAlessandro» / «Marie d’Alessandro», Vietnamese ơ ư (the horn at the right).
--   THE PRINCIPLE (unchanged, the coordinator's): the skeleton OVER-merges — twins only cost the sender one more line of context.
--   • the skeleton DROPS THE APOSTROPHE: «Pal’o» = «Palo», «O’Brien» = «OBrien», «’Αννα» = «Αννα»;
--   • tools/names/render_scan.py has a part 'beside' that draws every allowed letter with a mark next to its base letter (48 px, Poppins
--     and the system fonts, 400–700) and measures where the mark's ink lies: within the rows the letter covers — beside it, not above
--     or below — the letter gets the skeleton of its base letter (pixel-twins.txt, generated): «ľ» = «l», «ď» = «d», «ť» = «t»,
--     «Ά» = «Α», «ơ» = «o». So «Paľo», «Pal’o» and «Palo» are twins; nothing is refused that was allowed.
--   The rule is generated, identical in the live app, by tools/names/name_rule.mjs (Unicode 16.0.0 data in tools/names/).
--   EXISTING NAMES: no name changes (the normalised form is the sixth version's); every row is keyed again by this rule: more members
--   become twins (told apart by company, city or #handle), nobody is renamed or refused for it. The counts are printed (RAISE NOTICE).
-- Every function keeps its GRANT/REVOKE (0026). Safe to run twice.
-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

